    <name>Apollo 16 Particles and Fields Subsatellite</name>
    <type>Spacecraft</type>
    <naif_host_id>A16S</naif_host_id>
    <description>The Apollo 16 subsatellite (PFS-2) was a small spacecraft released into lunar orbit from the Apollo 16 Service Module. Its main objectives were to study the plasma, particle, and magnetic field environment of the Moon and map the lunar gravity field. The subsatellite orbited the Moon and returned data from 24 April until 29 May 1972. Because the initial orbit was not optimal, it decayed rapidly and the subsatellite prematurely impacted the Moon after 34 days (425 revolutions) in orbit.  </description>
